                        "form": "vraagtekentjes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b8dde0f9-b774-3030-9f8d-003341e74c23",
                        "entry_id": "bd059765-2fce-3fa6-a163-9d51ec5a3074",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een leesteken (?) dat men aan het eind van een zin plaatst om deze vragend te maken"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9650a13-37a5-43b9-a532-273fd2caa6bc",
                                "sense_id": "b8dde0f9-b774-3030-9f8d-003341e74c23",
                                "text": "Hij snapte die opdracht niet, dus zette hij er een paar vraagtekens bij."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d5860920-f904-3645-a05d-7c3e3f444895",
                        "entry_id": "bd059765-2fce-3fa6-a163-9d51ec5a3074",
                        "glosses": [
                            "twijfels hebben bij"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6152b3a-ed55-4d6b-8cce-c0e82d3e9e50",
                                "sense_id": "d5860920-f904-3645-a05d-7c3e3f444895",
                                "text": "Hij zette vraagtekens bij de verklaring van de getuige."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3cc670e-34c9-426c-8605-919d45891332",
                                "sense_id": "d5860920-f904-3645-a05d-7c3e3f444895",
                                "text": "In totaal zijn 25 politici aangeklaagd in Catalonië. De bekendste van deze groep, Carles Puigdemont, liet het Catalaanse Parlement de onafhankelijkheid van Catalonië uitroepen. Zondag is hij in en door Duitsland op Spaans bevel gearresteerd. Juridisch klopt dit misschien wel, maar er zijn vraagtekens."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bef1ff9d-7901-417c-9799-a9cbfce0c3f9",
                                "sense_id": "d5860920-f904-3645-a05d-7c3e3f444895",
                                "text": "Veel mensen zetten vraagtekens bij de grootte en de zogeheten hubfunctie van Schiphol."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9a0c3e38-876e-4bd7-bb9f-15a1fa85589d",
                        "source_entry_id": "bd059765-2fce-3fa6-a163-9d51ec5a3074",
                        "source_sense_id": "b8dde0f9-b774-3030-9f8d-003341e74c23",
                        "source_sense_description": "een leesteken (?) dat men aan het eind van een zin plaatst om deze vragend te maken",
                        "target_lang_word": "question mark",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "question mark",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2260748-bed0-3dcb-bfdd-75049d3da5cf",
                                        "entry_id": "a2a0595a-8fe3-301c-a706-50ca46291e1f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The punctuation mark \\\"?\\\", used at the end of a sentence to indicate a question."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3420c287-bb1b-441d-9249-120b3919ed53",
                                                "sense_id": "e2260748-bed0-3dcb-bfdd-75049d3da5cf",
                                                "text": "Do you see this curious-looking mark in the margin? It is a little crooked mark with a dot at the bottom of it. It is a question mark. It always comes at the end of questions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e8341ff-5fbb-4b23-8b07-74c66ac3beb5",
                                                "sense_id": "e2260748-bed0-3dcb-bfdd-75049d3da5cf",
                                                "text": "When you come to a question mark, you must stop and rest. If the question may be answered by yes or no, your voice must rise on the last word before the question mark."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6164a81f-c4e0-4911-a6dd-efbf6a788096",
                                                "sense_id": "e2260748-bed0-3dcb-bfdd-75049d3da5cf",
                                                "text": "As the relation of the faulted lamprophyre dike to faults 1 to 3 is not known, the intersection of the dike with these faults is shown on plate 13 with question marks."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6a359cb-5f87-428e-8a08-53872b40328b",
                                                "sense_id": "e2260748-bed0-3dcb-bfdd-75049d3da5cf",
                                                "text": "Fortunately, then, this text in which the play is preserved to us is, in general, substantively good. The quarto's punctuation and lineation, however, are much less reliable than its language. The pointing is not in most respects notably worse than that in comparable publications; but the text is peppered with question marks, the printers either having spilled these among the other marks or run out of periods."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c592d468-ef15-4ddc-a501-5a53248b8d04",
                                                "sense_id": "e2260748-bed0-3dcb-bfdd-75049d3da5cf",
                                                "text": "I would like to comment only on the question mark in the topic – and raise several questions for our discussion hidden within that question mark, questions integral to the ongoing debates since [John] Calvin, integral to the \"historically extended and socially embedded argument within the Reformed tradition about the very goods that constitute that tradition\" (adapting Alasdair MacIntyre's description of a living tradition)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee493eb3-2275-4aed-b673-46a57a67cce7",
                                                "sense_id": "e2260748-bed0-3dcb-bfdd-75049d3da5cf",
                                                "text": "The waitress, [...] places my coffee beside my notebook then stops to gawp at what I've written and a deep frown forms between her unplucked eyebrows. She stares at the initials, the connecting lines, the question marks, the circles. I see them as she sees them: a load of rubbish, fanciful nonsense from a person who has watched one too many cop shows."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af9e43de-5b64-33f0-9426-788ac1272c0f",
                                        "entry_id": "a2a0595a-8fe3-301c-a706-50ca46291e1f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state of doubt or uncertainty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d95b966c-3a96-4e6b-a4a3-fd0b4fb2b834",
                                                "sense_id": "af9e43de-5b64-33f0-9426-788ac1272c0f",
                                                "text": "There’s a question mark over whether or not he’ll be fit for the next game."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87efb256-5c7a-43e5-bc53-631edf7fc985",
                                                "sense_id": "af9e43de-5b64-33f0-9426-788ac1272c0f",
                                                "text": "Because I keep answering questions with more questions, and there are question marks between myself and other people and I can no longer keep myself from wondering why that must always be so."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4495deb8-2442-4523-ab2b-35f47105a38b",
                                                "sense_id": "af9e43de-5b64-33f0-9426-788ac1272c0f",
                                                "text": "Wherever the ambiguity in the Urfaustbook may have come from, and whether the author was fully aware of it or not, it is there: a faint, wavering question-mark at the end of an otherwise unequivocal statement that Faust was damned to all eternity in hell."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f84b62e-6cd6-4458-95c9-f93cddeb8e9c",
                                                "sense_id": "af9e43de-5b64-33f0-9426-788ac1272c0f",
                                                "text": "The Pachoutinsky brothers: Eugene, Anatol and Leon: what had become of them? had they survived the war? were they in want? All one big question mark in my mind."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57e22ebe-f2a7-4df3-bbe1-c87781f7a058",
                                                "sense_id": "af9e43de-5b64-33f0-9426-788ac1272c0f",
                                                "text": "It was vaguely felt that a clear perception of atomic realities would necessitate a complete intellectual revolution. Such a revolution was particularly unwelcome; it meant exchanging the certainties of conventional warfare for a vast number of question marks. The fact that it was others who possessed atomic weapons made the question marks still less attractive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d9777c7-5a7e-423d-a2d0-934311727ed8",
                                                "sense_id": "af9e43de-5b64-33f0-9426-788ac1272c0f",
                                                "text": "Dirk Kuyt sandwiched a goal in between [Andy] Carroll's double as City endured a night of total misery, with captain Carlos Tevez limping off early on with a hamstring strain that puts a serious question mark over his participation in Saturday's FA Cup semi-final against Manchester United at Wembley."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b8b5c2c-dd5d-4563-8f9c-19aa3baca90e",
                                                "sense_id": "af9e43de-5b64-33f0-9426-788ac1272c0f",
                                                "text": "[W]e see that intellectual pursuits always end with question marks. The curse of learning is that it leaves us with no answers to the questions that matter the most. That's because the answers to our existential questions are not found under the sun."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46a30f3c-623f-461b-8238-ae8b502fa65a",
                                                "sense_id": "af9e43de-5b64-33f0-9426-788ac1272c0f",
                                                "text": "For a while, the biggest question mark of allegiance is August Walker (Henry Cavill, subverting his man-of-steel screen presence), the brutish CIA tagalong feeding his superiors the theory that [Ethan] Hunt may really be going rogue after years of being left out in the cold by his handlers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "662ba1a4-fd6b-362b-96d5-5801000229fe",
                                        "entry_id": "a2a0595a-8fe3-301c-a706-50ca46291e1f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An enigmatic, inscrutable, or mysterious person or thing; an enigma, a riddle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96b5a0a3-2396-4d50-8564-6b3c9e938c54",
                                                "sense_id": "662ba1a4-fd6b-362b-96d5-5801000229fe",
                                                "text": "Let us admit that the Platonic dialogue is an enigma—something perplexing and to be wondered at. The Platonic dialogue is one big question mark."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "285cd733-2faf-4f8c-a98e-c3dce1fb278f",
                                                "sense_id": "662ba1a4-fd6b-362b-96d5-5801000229fe",
                                                "text": "Mr. [Richard] Foreman has been the reigning philosopher vaudevillian of the New York avant-garde for three decades now, creating fractured dreamscapes in which life is the banana cream pie that keeps hitting you in the face. His starting point is that the world is unknowable, self is a question mark, and existence is one long chain of frustrations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5bb0260-f128-4211-89f0-a09c63afbd41",
                                                "sense_id": "662ba1a4-fd6b-362b-96d5-5801000229fe",
                                                "text": "Those who enroll in my class are English majors seeking a license to teach at the secondary level. To most of them, middle school is a question mark, unexplored territory about which they have mixed feelings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2ceabbe-d53d-3904-b316-aec5c407ecdb",
                                        "entry_id": "a2a0595a-8fe3-301c-a706-50ca46291e1f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Polygonia interrogationis, a North American nymphalid butterfly with a silver mark on the underside of its hindwing resembling a question mark (sense 1)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f345a61a-714c-434c-ac34-b8634488e164",
                                                "sense_id": "d2ceabbe-d53d-3904-b316-aec5c407ecdb",
                                                "text": "Question Mark (Polygonia interrogationis). Preferred host plants are elms (Ulmus spp.), hackberry (Celtis spp.), hops (Humulus spp.), nettle (Urtica spp.), and false nettle (Boehmeria cylindrica)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5848b2e-ee11-43e3-a7cb-5f13bea91926",
                                                "sense_id": "d2ceabbe-d53d-3904-b316-aec5c407ecdb",
                                                "text": "Commas (Polygonia comma) and Question Marks (Polygonia interrogationis) occur from the Gulf Coast to Canada and west to the Rockies. [...] Question Marks and Commas are handsome butterflies with burnt orange and black markings. [...] On the underside of each hind wing of the Comma is a small, distinctive silver hook that resembles a comma. The Question Mark has a small silver dot just below the hook—a question mark. Any other name just wouldn't do."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6b864f3-48f3-4965-86e0-9822bbc61730",
                                                "sense_id": "d2ceabbe-d53d-3904-b316-aec5c407ecdb",
                                                "text": "Other members of this genus that are frequently encountered in the park are the eastern comma (P. comma) and question mark (P. interrogationis)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "question mark",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "17abc593-9bfb-33a6-bc9e-963c9f1e6376",
                                        "entry_id": "6cf174a7-29e9-3173-b965-16e861e7f7ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Final interrogative particle, expressing second-guessing, usually in an exaggerated, rising tone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f61398f2-6d38-453d-9677-dfcf34c6a074",
                                                "sense_id": "17abc593-9bfb-33a6-bc9e-963c9f1e6376",
                                                "text": "All real discovery comes from the ?, the basic curiosity and acceptance of, “Well, we think subatomic particles might exist, at least they have a tendency to exist, but we really don’t know for sure, you know, question mark?”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "261b4c49-4f3e-4f4b-9b23-dee91a21c8e8",
                                                "sense_id": "17abc593-9bfb-33a6-bc9e-963c9f1e6376",
                                                "text": "So I see one movement towards a new kind of society, a new kind of mobility. So am I right, question mark?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "226fceb4-08f3-4db9-938c-9c1d21348af9",
                                                "sense_id": "17abc593-9bfb-33a6-bc9e-963c9f1e6376",
                                                "text": "And is it like open? Can like anybody join, question mark?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
